Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:34:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] UefiPayloadPkg: Hide boot options on chosen USB ports

Some platforms have onboard USB devices that enumerate as mass storage
but are not boot media.

Add PcdBootHiddenUsbPorts and PcdBootHiddenUsbPci. When any port bit
is set, PlatformBootManagerLib installs an
EDKII_PLATFORM_BOOT_MANAGER_PROTOCOL whose RefreshAllBootOptions()
drops boot options for PciRoot()/Pci(Dev,Fn)/USB(Port,...) on that
controller and port, and deletes matching Boot#### variables,
including ones BDS did not create. The devices stay usable from the
shell and the OS.

PcdBootHiddenUsbPci defaults to 00:14.0, the PCH xHCI on Intel
platforms.

